  "delivered": [
    "EntityPool admits logical entities by pool capacity, reuses inactive nodes and shares a frame activation budget across prefab keys. Repeated frame IDs do not reset the allowance; failed attempts consume it.",
    "Shared AssetCatalog keeps AssetPlan and EntityPool quality/LOD selection aligned. Optional detail-layers.hideAtLod rows use registered prefab addresses and hide from the selected LOD onward; malformed or unknown rows fail before loading.",
    "LOD/quality/despawn/close invalidate obsolete jobs by bucket identity, abort pending loads, and release late leases without activating. Hidden entities retain admission, downgrades preserve oldest admissions, failed loads retry explicitly.",
    "Cocos adapter uses AssetLease, inactive instantiation, one shared material per source and instancing capability, monotonic AFTER_UPDATE subscription, and AFTER_DRAW retirement before returning references. Realtime skinning never enables instancing here; baked grouping remains SC4.",
    "Inactive nodes hold the prefab lease until eviction, incompatible transition or close. Billboard allocations enabled on reuse retire at eviction even when other nodes still use the prefab.",
    "Stage3dDevScene exposes an inspector/preview 500-spawn toggle; medium admits 300 at 8/frame, high 500 at 16/frame, low skips the details pool. Old SC0 mixed-page fixtures are preserved."
  ],
